    "problem": "Gaps in the climate record of East Asian monsoon history over the past two interglacial-glacial cycles have hampered the ability to test ideas about orbital- and millennial-scale controls and relationships between the monsoon and climate in other regions.",
    "method": "The authors construct a continuous 224,000-year record of the East Asian monsoon by analyzing absolute-dated oxygen isotopes in Sanbao cave stalagmites, filling previous gaps in the paleoclimate record to better understand its long-term drivers.",
    "task": "The task is to construct a complete, 224,000-year, absolute-dated record of East Asian monsoon strength from Chinese cave deposits to analyze its orbital- and millennial-scale controls and relationship to global climate changes.",
